	)
	(text_box "Requirements:\n\nTo flash the firmware, the MCU must enter bootloader mode. For this, it is necessary to activate the BOOT0 input (active high) and then reset it. Since the MCU has the power input under control, before entering the bootloader mode it is necessary to ensure that there is no power interruption, so the SOFT_PWR output will need to remain active. It is also necessary to disable CM5 from going to sleep/reset, so ~{PWR_BTN} will have to remain high.\n\nSequence for programming the SYSMCU:\n\n- CM5 sends SYSMCU command to shut down all modules.\n- Disable the watchdog by setting WDG_SET to LOW.\n- UART_TX/DOUT1 is set to LOW.\n- DIB_OE_SYNC is set to LOW.\n- ~{DIB1_CSA} is set to LOW and ~{SYSMCU_CS} is set to LOW. This will enable the D flip-flop.\n- CM5 generates short positive pulse on DIB_OE_SYNC. This will latch SOFT_PWR (active high) to ensure power delivery without interruption and set BOOT0 (active high) and also shutdown all DIB peripheral modules via ~{DIB_SHUTDOWN}.\n- UART_TX/DOUT1 is set HIGH which will reset the SYSMCU via ~{WDG_MR} and put it into bootloader mode as BOOT0 is now active.\n- The firmware programming procedure starts.\n- When programming is complete, display a message on the screen that the device will be powered down. Set ~{DIB1_CSA} to HIGH and ~{SYSMCU_CS} to HIGH. This will turn off the power. \n\nNote: During programming of SYSMCU, it is necessary to ensure that CM5 is not reset or powered down. For this purpose, a 1G57 is used configured as a 2-Input NAND gate with inverted B input so that the signals ~{RPI_PWR_ON} and ~{RESET_OUT} have no effect on the ~{PWR_BTN} input of CM5 as long as the flip-flop is latched.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 81.28 0)
		(size 83.82 43.7324)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.889 0.889)
				(color 132 0 132 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f05574ba-8bd6-427a-890f-351f3a4a96f9")
	)
